Tic-Tac-Toe AI using Minimax Algorithm


This project is a command-line based Tic-Tac-Toe game implemented in Python, where a human player competes against an intelligent AI agent. The AI uses the Minimax algorithm, a classic decision-making technique in game theory, to always choose the optimal move.
The game is played on a 3×3 grid, where the user plays as 'X' and the AI plays as 'O'. The program evaluates all possible future game states and ensures that the AI either wins or forces a draw, making it unbeatable.

Features
Interactive CLI-based gameplay
AI opponent powered by Minimax algorithm
Optimal move selection ensuring no loss
Win, loss, and draw detection
Input validation for smooth user experience

Technologies Used
Python
Standard libraries (math)

Objective
The goal of this project is to demonstrate the practical implementation of the Minimax algorithm in artificial intelligence and understand how decision-making works in turn-based games.

How to Play
Run the script in a Python environment
Enter positions from 0 to 8 corresponding to the grid
Try to beat the AI (Hint: you can’t)
